 "cards": [
  {
   "key": "whats_going_on",
   "title": "What's going on",
   "text": "A paper reports that Krabbe disease is caused by changes in a gene called GALC [E6e63617]. A paper reports that this gene is normally needed to break down a fatty substance that is part of the material protecting nerves, called myelin [Ee586157]. A paper reports that without enough of this enzyme working, a toxic substance called psychosine builds up and harms the cells that protect nerves [Eecc2812]. A paper also reports that Krabbe disease happens because of a missing enzyme inside tiny cell parts called lysosomes, which normally help break things down, so this is called a lysosomal enzyme deficiency [E050a41e]. A paper reports that this leads to loss and damage of the myelin covering around nerves, called demyelination [E8b1c4df]. A paper reports that it also causes swelling and irritation in the nervous system, called neuroinflammation [E5aaac6b].",
   "citations": [
    "E6e63617",
    "Ee586157",
    "Eecc2812",
    "E050a41e",
    "E8b1c4df",
    "E5aaac6b"
   ],
   "status": "ok"
  },
  {
   "key": "similar",
   "title": "Other diseases that share this biology",
   "text": "According to Reactome, the GALC gene and the genes behind several other diseases all work in the body's pathway for breaking down fatty substances called glycosphingolipids [E6be1459, E41520eb]. A paper reports that Gaucher disease also involves fatty substances building up in cells because of a missing lysosomal enzyme, the same kind of problem as Krabbe [E3f6bbf0, Ec8d1187, E60744b8, E309fa8a]. A paper reports that Fabry disease shares this same pattern of a missing lysosomal enzyme and fat buildup in cells [E4b5796e, Ee0e2214]. A paper reports that some late-onset forms of Parkinson's disease also involve a missing enzyme and fat buildup similar to Krabbe's disease process [Ece278e5, E8b12886]. According to HPO, children with GM2 AB variant can have some of the same signs as Krabbe, such as low muscle tone, stiff muscles, and loss of brain function over time [Ebb770bf, E3b6cdca, E0936c1c, E6b7d4d8, E861bd0e, Ef793a01]. A paper reports that metachromatic leukodystrophy, also called MLD, is caused by a different missing lysosomal enzyme but leads to similar fat buildup and nerve-covering damage as Krabbe [E2af53d8, Ef9f74f4]. According to HPO, children with MLD and Krabbe can both have increased protein in their spinal fluid and slower nerve signal speed [E8f41824, E1e675ab, E13dd0cf, E3abe212].",
   "citations": [
